## Electromagnet sample: simple C-yoke (quarter model) with Kelvin spheres
##
## Required labels:
##   block 1 = "iron"        (the C-shaped yoke, three brick volumes)
##   block 2 = "air"         (the inner air sphere around the yoke)
##   block 3 = "kelvin"      (the exterior Kelvin image sphere)
##   sideset 1 = "kelvin_int" (inner sphere outer surface)
##   sideset 2 = "kelvin_ext" (exterior sphere outer surface)
##
## Geometry (XZ symmetry quarter model — symmetry planes applied by panel):
##   Iron yoke: 3 bricks in z>0 region
##   Inner air sphere: R = 0.060 m at origin
##   Exterior Kelvin sphere: R = 0.060 m, offset 0.200 m in +x
##
## Build policy:
##   1. SUBTRACT iron from inner air half BEFORE imprint+merge
##      (nested merge alone does NOT share surfaces)
##   2. Webcut both spheres with zplane to create anchor curves so the
##      `radia_export netgen` C++ plugin can pair the kelvin_int / kelvin_ext
##      surface mesh nodes 1:1 (Periodic Kelvin)

reset

# === 1. Iron yoke (3 bricks in z > 0) ===
brick x 0.0125 y 0.040 z 0.050
move volume 1 x 0.00625 y 0.020 z 0.025

brick x 0.0125 y 0.080 z 0.025
move volume 2 x 0.00625 y 0.080 z 0.0125

brick x 0.0125 y 0.0625 z 0.0525
move volume 3 x 0.00625 y 0.15125 z 0.02625

# === 2. Spheres: inner (vol 4) at origin, kelvin (vol 5) at offset ===
create sphere radius 0.060
create sphere radius 0.060
move volume 5 x 0.200

# === 3. Webcut both spheres with zplane (creates anchor curves on equator) ===
# After webcut: vol 4 = inner top (z>0), vol 6 = inner bot (z<0),
#               vol 5 = kelvin top, vol 7 = kelvin bot
webcut volume 4 5 with plane zplane

# === 4. Subtract iron from inner top (iron only sits in z>0) ===
# inner bot has no iron to subtract.
subtract volume 1 2 3 from volume 4 keep_tool

# === 5. Imprint + merge for shared interfaces and equator nodes ===
imprint volume 4 6
merge volume 4 6
imprint volume 5 7
merge volume 5 7
imprint volume 1 2 3 4
merge volume 1 2 3 4

# === 6. Mesh ===
volume 1 2 3 scheme tetmesh
volume 1 2 3 size 0.005
mesh volume 1 2 3

volume 4 6 scheme tetmesh
volume 4 6 size 0.012
mesh volume 4 6

volume 5 7 scheme tetmesh
volume 5 7 size 0.012
mesh volume 5 7

# === 7. Blocks ===
block 1 add volume 1 2 3
block 1 name "iron"
block 2 add volume 4 6
block 2 name "air"
block 3 add volume 5 7
block 3 name "kelvin"

# Hide air + kelvin for visibility
volume 4 5 6 7 visibility off
